From 647076c7a3e641a7c4ed41d8d922186d0e17754a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 09:58:22 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Kernels: stiffness matrices and action of the tangent
 operator computed without forming the operator B

The non-zero entries of the block of a node of the operator B are described,
for each kind of gradients, by a constexpr table (getBOperatorEntries),
checked at compile time against computeB. The products K B_b and
B_a^T (K B_b) of the stiffness matrices (kernel, host version, derivative
of the heat flux with respect to the temperature) and the products of the
action of the tangent operator without assembly use this table instead of
forming B: the zero entries are skipped, the other terms are added in the
same order, and the results are the same for finite values (except the
sign of zero results of underflowing products with contracted
multiplications and additions). The diagonal kernels only compute the
diagonal of the blocks.

Finite strain in 3D: 254 registers and 576 bytes of stack per thread
before, 64 and 72 after; small strain in 3D: 126 and 576 before, 80 and
72 after. Assembly 1.1 to 3.1 times faster on one CPU core, 1.4 to 1.9
times on a GPU; heat transfer 6 % slower on a GPU (84 registers instead
of 64).
